# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key to this problem is a mathematical operator—the Hamiltonian, which "
"represents the total energy of a system. For computational purposes, we can "
"think of this Hamiltonian as a large matrix. The solutions we are looking "
"for—specifically the system's ground state—are the lowest eigenvalues of "
"this matrix. The challenge, however, is that for practical problems, this "
"Hamiltonian matrix is very large. It grows exponentially with the size of "
"the system, quickly becoming too big ($2^n$ where $n$ is the number of "
"qubits) for even the most powerful supercomputers to store or solve "
"directly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang susi sa problemang ito ay isang mathematical operator — ang Hamiltonian,"
" na kumakatawan sa kabuuang enerhiya ng isang sistema. Para sa computational"
" na layunin, maaari nating isipin ang Hamiltonian na ito bilang isang "
"malaking matrix. Ang mga solusyong hinahanap natin — lalo na ang ground "
"state ng sistema — ay ang pinakamababang eigenvalue ng matrix na ito. Ang "
"hamon, gayunpaman, ay para sa mga praktikal na problema, napakalaki ng "
"Hamiltonian matrix na ito. Lumalaki ito nang exponential ayon sa laki ng "
"sistema, at mabilis na nagiging masyadong malaki ($2^n$ kung saan $n$ ang "
"bilang ng mga qubit) para maiimbak o malutas nang direkta kahit ng "
"pinakamakapangyarihang supercomputer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"H_{0,0} & H_{0,1} & \\cdots & H_{0,N-1} \\\\\n"
"H_{1,0} & H_{1,1} & \\cdots & H_{1,N-1} \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"H_{N-1,0} & H_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & H_{N-1,N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\quad (N=2^n)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"H_{0,0} & H_{0,1} & \\cdots & H_{0,N-1} \\\\\n"
"H_{1,0} & H_{1,1} & \\cdots & H_{1,N-1} \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"H_{N-1,0} & H_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & H_{N-1,N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\quad (N=2^n)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get around this, we use a powerful strategy known as the subspace method."
" Instead of tackling the whole matrix, we intelligently select a small, "
"relevant slice — a \"subspace\" — that we believe contains the most "
"important information about the low-energy solution we're looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang malutas ito, gumagamit tayo ng isang makapangyarihang estratehiya na "
"tinatawag na subspace method. Sa halip na harapin ang buong matrix, maingat "
"tayong pumipili ng maliit at makabuluhang bahagi — isang \"subspace\" — na "
"naniniwala tayong naglalaman ng pinakamahalagang impormasyon tungkol sa "
"mababang-enerhiyang solusyong hinahanap natin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Full Hamiltonian}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\cdots & H_{i,j} & \\cdots \\\\\n"
"& \\vdots & \\ddots\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Project}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Projected Hamiltonian}}{\\tilde{H}}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle b_1 | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_1 | H | b_L \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\langle b_L | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_L | H | b_L \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Diagonalize}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Eigenvalues}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"E_0 & & 0 \\\\\n"
"& \\ddots & \\\\\n"
"0 & & E_{L-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Full Hamiltonian}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\cdots & H_{i,j} & \\cdots \\\\\n"
"& \\vdots & \\ddots\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Project}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Projected Hamiltonian}}{\\tilde{H}}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle b_1 | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_1 | H | b_L \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\langle b_L | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_L | H | b_L \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Diagonalize}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Eigenvalues}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"E_0 & & 0 \\\\\n"
"& \\ddots & \\\\\n"
"0 & & E_{L-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once this small subspace is defined by a set of basis states "
"$\\{|b_i\\rangle\\}$, the full Hamiltonian is projected onto it to create "
"the new, smaller matrix $\\tilde{H}$. Each element of this matrix is "
"calculated from the subspace basis states and the original Hamiltonian as in"
" $\\langle b_i | H | b_j \\rangle$. This small matrix can then be easily "
"diagonalized on a classical computer, and the resulting eigenvalues are our "
"estimated energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag natukoy na ang maliit na subspace na ito sa pamamagitan ng isang set "
"ng basis states na $\\{|b_i\\rangle\\}$, ini-project ang buong Hamiltonian "
"dito upang lumikha ng bagong, mas maliit na matrix na $\\tilde{H}$. Ang "
"bawat elemento ng matrix na ito ay kinakalkula mula sa mga basis state ng "
"subspace at sa orihinal na Hamiltonian tulad ng sa $\\langle b_i | H | b_j "
"\\rangle$. Ang maliit na matrix na ito ay madaling ma-diagonalize sa isang "
"klasikal na computer, at ang mga resultang eigenvalue ay ang ating "
"tinantyang mga enerhiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As you might guess, the success of this entire approach heavily relies on "
"choosing a \"good\" subspace. If our subspace does not accurately represent "
"the true ground state, our final answer will be incorrect. This is where "
"quantum computers come in: they allow us to prepare and sample from complex "
"quantum states designed to identify these important subspaces. For truly "
"massive problems, like complex chemical structures or binding sites, even "
"the projected matrix may still be challenging to diagonalize. Thus, such "
"problems are ideally-suited to leverage the strengths of both quantum and "
"classical computing resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng maaari mong hulaan, ang tagumpay ng buong pamamaraang ito ay lubos "
"na nakasalalay sa pagpili ng isang \"magandang\" subspace. Kung hindi tumpak"
" na kinakatawan ng ating subspace ang tunay na ground state, ang ating "
"panghuling sagot ay magiging mali. Dito pumapasok ang mga quantum computer: "
"pinapayagan nila tayong maghanda at mag-sample mula sa mga kumplikadong "
"quantum state na idinisenyo upang matukoy ang mga mahahalagang subspace na "
"ito. Para sa tunay na napakalaking mga problema, tulad ng mga kumplikadong "
"istruktura ng kemikal o mga binding site, maaaring mahirap pa ring "
"i-diagonalize ang projected matrix. Kaya naman, ang ganitong mga problema ay"
" perpektong angkop para pagsamahin ang mga kalakasan ng parehong quantum at "
"klasikal na computing resources.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following sections, we will explore two advanced algorithms, SQD and "
"SKQD, which leverage quantum mechanics to find and construct these "
"subspaces. For a deeper dive, there is a [full-length "
"course](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) on IBM Quantum"
" learning devoted to these topics in detail. For our purposes in this "
"course, we will keep the explanation at a high level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga sumusunod na seksyon, tutuklasin natin ang dalawang advanced na "
"algorithm — SQD at SKQD — na gumagamit ng quantum mechanics upang mahanap at"
" maitayo ang mga subspace na ito. Para sa mas malalim na pag-aaral, may "
"[buong kurso](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) sa IBM "
"Quantum learning na nakatuon sa mga paksang ito nang detalyado. Para sa "
"ating layunin sa kursong ito, pananatilihin natin ang paliwanag sa mataas na"
" antas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample-based Quantum Diagonalization {#sample-based-quantum-diagonalization}"
msgstr ""
"Sample-based Quantum Diagonalization {#sample-based-quantum-diagonalization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample-based Quantum Diagonalization (SQD) is a powerful variational "
"algorithm that implements the subspace method in a quantum way. It avoids "
"costly, complex procedures like Hadamard tests by using a quantum computer "
"to prepare a trial state and sample *bitstrings*, which define the subspace "
"for classical diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Sample-based Quantum Diagonalization (SQD) ay isang makapangyarihang "
"variational algorithm na nagpapatupad ng subspace method sa quantum na "
"paraan. Iniiwasan nito ang mga mahal at kumplikadong pamamaraan tulad ng "
"Hadamard tests sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng quantum computer upang maghanda"
" ng trial state at mag-sample ng mga *bitstring*, na nagtatakda ng subspace "
"para sa klasikal na diagonalization.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A schematic of the workflow specific to sample-based quantum "
"diagonalization. The steps include a variational quantum circuit, using "
"measurements to project the Hamiltonian into a subspace, then using a "
"classical optimizer to update variational parameters in the circuit and "
"repeating.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-"
"performance-computing/sqd-skqd/sqd-cycle.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A schematic of the workflow specific to sample-based quantum "
"diagonalization. The steps include a variational quantum circuit, using "
"measurements to project the Hamiltonian into a subspace, then using a "
"classical optimizer to update variational parameters in the circuit and "
"repeating.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-"
"performance-computing/sqd-skqd/sqd-cycle.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The SQD algorithm can be broken down into the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Maaaring hatiin ang SQD algorithm sa mga sumusunod na hakbang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Prepare the Ansatz state {#step-1-prepare-the-ansatz-state}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: Ihanda ang Ansatz state {#step-1-prepare-the-ansatz-state}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $H = \\sum_{j=1}^Q \\alpha_j P_j$ be the Hamiltonian on $n$ qubits. "
"While the true ground state may be supported on all $2^n$ basis states, SQD "
"is most effective in instances where the ground state can be well-"
"approximated by a sparse subspace (a polynomially-sized set of "
"bitstrings).\n"
msgstr ""
"Hayaan nating $H = \\sum_{j=1}^Q \\alpha_j P_j$ ang Hamiltonian sa $n$ na "
"qubit. Kahit ang tunay na ground state ay maaaring suportado sa lahat ng "
"$2^n$ na basis state, pinaka-epektibo ang SQD sa mga sitwasyon kung saan ang"
" ground state ay maaaring mahusay na ma-approximate ng isang maliit na "
"subspace (isang polynomial-sized na set ng mga bitstring).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To construct this subspace, we start with an input state $|\\phi_0\\rangle$,"
" such as the Hartree-Fock (HF) state in chemistry. We then apply a "
"parameterized quantum circuit, $U(\\theta)$, which is known as the ansatz.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang maitayo ang subspace na ito, nagsisimula tayo sa isang input state na "
"$|\\phi_0\\rangle$, tulad ng Hartree-Fock (HF) state sa kimika. Pagkatapos "
"ay nag-aaplay tayo ng isang parameterized quantum circuit, $U(\\theta)$, na "
"kilala bilang ang ansatz.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing the overlap of the computational basis states making up "
"the ansatz and those making up the true ground state. Specifically, the "
"image shows that the two regions will have some overlap, but might not "
"perfectly match.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-"
"performance-computing/sqd-skqd/ansatz.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A diagram showing the overlap of the computational basis states making up "
"the ansatz and those making up the true ground state. Specifically, the "
"image shows that the two regions will have some overlap, but might not "
"perfectly match.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-"
"performance-computing/sqd-skqd/ansatz.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This diagram illustrates the goal of a good ansatz. The ansatz prepares a "
"quantum state whose support (the set of basis states it is composed of) "
"should ideally have a large overlap with the support of the true ground "
"state. This circuit allows us to quickly project the ansatz onto "
"computational basis states, which will be further used in classical "
"diagonalization. In other words: we don't have to guess an ansatz that is "
"the ground state; we only need it to contain the same basis states. Then "
"classical diagonalization of the projected Hamiltonian will give us the "
"superposition of basis states that best approximates the ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilalarawan ng diagram na ito ang layunin ng isang magandang ansatz. "
"Inihahanda ng ansatz ang isang quantum state na ang suporta (ang set ng mga "
"basis state na binubuo nito) ay dapat na may malaking overlap sa suporta ng "
"tunay na ground state. Pinapayagan tayo ng circuit na ito na mabilis na "
"i-project ang ansatz sa mga computational basis state, na gagamitin pa sa "
"klasikal na diagonalization. Sa madaling salita: hindi natin kailangang "
"hulaan ang isang ansatz na siya mismo ang ground state; kailangan lang "
"nitong maglaman ng parehong mga basis state. Pagkatapos, ang klasikal na "
"diagonalization ng projected Hamiltonian ang magbibigay sa atin ng "
"superposition ng mga basis state na pinakamalapit sa ground state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Sample the subspace {#step-2-sample-the-subspace}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-sample ang subspace {#step-2-sample-the-subspace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By sampling from the circuit prepared by the ansatz, we get a collection of "
"bitstrings, $\\{b_j\\}_{j=1}^L$. These bitstrings define the basis of our "
"chosen subspace. The quantum runtime for this step is determined by the "
"depth of the circuit and the number of samples taken.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pamamagitan ng pag-sample mula sa circuit na inihanda ng ansatz, "
"nakakakuha tayo ng koleksyon ng mga bitstring, $\\{b_j\\}_{j=1}^L$. Ang mga "
"bitstring na ito ang nagtatakda ng basis ng ating piniling subspace. Ang "
"quantum runtime para sa hakbang na ito ay tinutukoy ng depth ng circuit at "
"ng bilang ng mga sample na kinuha.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Project and diagonalize classically {#step-3-project-and-"
"diagonalize-classically}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 3: I-project at i-diagonalize nang klasikal {#step-3-project-and-"
"diagonalize-classically}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the sampled bitstrings, we project the Hamiltonian into the subspace "
"they span. For each pair of bitstrings $(j, k)$, we classically compute the "
"matrix element $\\tilde{H}_{jk} = \\langle b_j | H | b_k \\rangle$. Because "
"Pauli operators are sparse, this step is classically efficient for physical "
"Hamiltonians. The resulting small matrix $\\tilde{H}$ is then diagonalized "
"on a classical processor to estimate the ground state and its energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang mga na-sample na bitstring, ini-project natin ang Hamiltonian sa "
"subspace na kanilang sinasaglaw. Para sa bawat pares ng mga bitstring $(j, "
"k)$, klasikal na kinakalkula natin ang matrix element na $\\tilde{H}_{jk} = "
"\\langle b_j | H | b_k \\rangle$. Dahil sparse ang mga Pauli operator, ang "
"hakbang na ito ay klasikal na mahusay para sa mga pisikal na Hamiltonian. "
"Ang resultang maliit na matrix na $\\tilde{H}$ ay idi-diagonalize pagkatapos"
" sa isang klasikal na processor upang matantya ang ground state at ang "
"enerhiya nito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Optimize the ansatz (optional) {#step-4-optimize-the-ansatz-"
"optional}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 4: I-optimize ang ansatz (opsyonal) {#step-4-optimize-the-ansatz-"
"optional}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The process can be made iterative. By treating the estimated ground state "
"energy as a cost function, we can optimize the circuit parameters "
"($\\theta$) by using methods like gradient descent to improve the ansatz, "
"and in turn, the energy approximation in the next iteration.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring gawing iterative ang proseso. Sa pamamagitan ng pagtrato sa "
"tinantyang ground state energy bilang isang cost function, maaari nating "
"i-optimize ang mga parameter ng circuit ($\\theta$) gamit ang mga pamamaraan"
" tulad ng gradient descent upang mapabuti ang ansatz, at sa gayon, ang "
"energy approximation sa susunod na iteration.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key advantages of SQD {#key-advantages-of-sqd}"
msgstr "Mga pangunahing kalamangan ng SQD {#key-advantages-of-sqd}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SQD offers several powerful features that make it a leading candidate for "
"demonstrating quantum advantage:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nag-aalok ang SQD ng ilang makapangyarihang katangian na nagpapaging "
"nangungunang kandidato para sa pagpapakita ng quantum advantage:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Strong robustness to noise: Suppose the true ground state is supported on "
"only two bitstrings. If these are sampled at all, even if their overlap with"
" our ansatz is small, the diagonalization will assign them the appropriate "
"weights and effectively ignore all other extraneous, noisy bitstrings that "
"might have also been sampled. This inherent filtering makes SQD particularly"
" noise-tolerant.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matibay na katatagan sa ingay: Ipagpalagay na ang tunay na ground state ay "
"suportado lamang sa dalawang bitstring. Kung ma-sample ang mga ito, kahit "
"maliit ang kanilang overlap sa ating ansatz, itatalaga ng diagonalization "
"ang tamang timbang sa kanila at epektibong bababalewalain ang lahat ng iba "
"pang labis at maingay na bitstring na maaaring na-sample din. Ang likas na "
"pag-filter na ito ang nagpapaging partikular na tolerante sa ingay ang "
"SQD.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Classical verifiability: Unlike QPE or VQAs, SQD yields a classical "
"approximation to the ground state. This means anyone with access to the list"
" of bitstrings and their weights can recompute and verify the energy "
"estimate directly on a classical computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Klasikal na paberipikasyon: Hindi tulad ng QPE o VQA, ang SQD ay nagbubunga "
"ng isang klasikal na approximation sa ground state. Nangangahulugan ito na "
"ang sinumang may access sa listahan ng mga bitstring at ang kanilang mga "
"timbang ay maaaring muling kalkulahin at i-verify ang energy estimate nang "
"direkta sa isang klasikal na computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SQD has already been used to estimate the ground-state dissociation energy "
"of N$_2$ and the electronic properties of [2Fe-2S] and [4Fe-4S] clusters "
"[[2]](#references), with circuits as large as 77 qubits and 10,570 gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginamit na ang SQD upang tantiyahin ang ground-state dissociation energy ng "
"N$_2$ at ang mga electronic property ng [2Fe-2S] at [4Fe-4S] cluster "
"[[2]](#references), na may mga circuit na kasinlaki ng 77 qubit at 10,570 "
"gate.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Subukan ang iyong pag-unawa {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "True or False: SQD can be applied to chemical systems.\n"
msgstr "Tama o Mali: Maaaring ilapat ang SQD sa mga kemikal na sistema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
